        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 9 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-31\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator built from scratch without external dependencies. The validator uses a two-phase approach: a lexer tokenizes the input file, then a parser validates the token stream against YAML 1.2 syntax rules. The architecture prioritizes simplicity, clear error reporting, and alignment with existing project patterns.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation types, no dependencies\n2. [T2] - Lexer depends only on types\n3. [T3, T5] - Parser needs lexer; lexer tests need lexer (independent of each other)\n4. [T4, T6] - CLI needs parser; parser tests need parser (independent of each other)\n5. [T7] - Integration tests require complete CLI\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (data: lexer uses Token, Position types)\n- T3 -> T2 (interface: parser consumes Token[] from lexer)\n- T4 -> T3 (interface: CLI calls parser validate function)\n- T5 -> T2 (build: tests import lexer module)\n- T6 -> T3 (build: tests import parser module)\n- T7 -> T4 (build: integration tests run CLI)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3 -> T4 -> T7\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation Types\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create type definitions for YAML validator in `src/yaml/types.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-type-definitions-srcyamltypests](design.md#31-type-definitions-srcyamltypests)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Position interface defined with line, column, and offset fields\n    - [ ] TokenType union type defined with all 16 token types (DOCUMENT_START, DOCUMENT_END, MAPPING_KEY, MAPPING_VALUE, SEQUENCE_ENTRY, SCALAR, QUOTED_SCALAR, LITERAL_BLOCK, FOLDED_BLOCK, ANCHOR, ALIAS, TAG, INDENT, NEWLINE, COMMENT, EOF)\n    -