        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/6f34a28f/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator/design.md",
        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Created**: 2026-01-31\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design describes a command-line YAML syntax validator built from scratch without external dependencies. The validator uses a two-phase approach: a lexer tokenizes the input file, then a parser validates the token stream against YAML 1.2 syntax rules. The architecture prioritizes simplicity, clear error reporting, and alignment with existing project patterns.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph CLI\n        A[validate-yaml.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Parser\n        B[lexer.ts]\n        C[parser.ts]\n        D[types.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph IO\n        E[File System]\n        F[stdout]\n        G[stderr]\n    end\n\n    E -->|read| A\n    A -->|content| B\n    B -->|tokens| C\n    C -->|result| A\n    A -->|success| F\n    A -->|errors| G\n    D -.->|types| B\n    D -.->|types| C\n```\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Overview\n\nThe solution consists of four main components:\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| CLI Entry | `src/cli/validate-yaml.ts` | Argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, exit codes |\n| Lexer | `src/yaml/lexer.ts` | Tokenizes YAML input, tracks line/column positions |\n| Parser | `src/yaml/parser.ts` | Validates token stream against YAML syntax rules |\n| Types | `src/yaml/types.ts` | Shared type definitions for tokens, errors, results |\n\n### 2.2 Data Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI\n    participant FS as File System\n    participant Lexer\n    participant Parser\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run src/cli/validate-yaml.ts <file>\n    CLI->>FS: Read file contents\n    FS-->>CLI: File content (string)\n    CLI->>Lexer: tokenize(content)\n\n    alt Lexer Error\n        Lexer-->>CLI: LexerError with line/column\n        CLI->>User: stderr: error message\n        CLI->>User: exit(1)\n    else Success\n        Lexer-->>CLI: Token[]\n        CLI->>Parser: validate(tokens)\n\n        alt Parser Error\n            Parser-->>CLI: ParseError with line/column\n            CLI->>User: stderr: error message\n            CLI->>User: exit(1)\n        else Valid\n            Parser-->>CLI: ValidationResult (success)\n            CLI->>User: stdout: success message\n            CLI->>User: exit(0)\n        end\n    end\n```\n\n### 2.3 Module Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  cli/\n    validate-yaml.ts      # CLI entry point\n  yaml/\n    types.ts              # Type definitions\n    lexer.ts              # Tokenizer\n    parser.ts             # Syntax validator\n    lexer.test.ts         # Lexer unit tests\n    parser.test.ts        # Parser unit tests\n  index.ts                # Existing entry (unchanged)\n  utils.ts                # Existing utils (unchanged)\n  utils.test.ts           # Existing tests (unchanged)\n```\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Type Definitions (`src/yaml/types.ts`)\n\n```typescript\n// Position tracking for error reporting\nexport interface Position {\n  line: number;    // 1-indexed\n  column: number;  // 1-indexed\n  offset: number;  // 0-indexed byte offset\n}\n\n// Token types produced by lexer\nexport type TokenType =\n  | \"DOCUMENT_START\"     // ---\n  | \"DOCUMENT_END\"       // ...\n  | \"MAPPING_KEY\"        // key:\n  | \"MAPPING_VALUE\"      // : (after key)\n  | \"SEQUENCE_ENTRY\"     // - (list item)\n  | \"SCALAR\"             // string, number, boolean, null\n  | \"QUOTED_SCALAR\"      // \"string\" or 'string'\n  | \"LITERAL_BLOCK\"      // |\n  | \"FOLDED_BLOCK\"       // >\n  | \"ANCHOR\"             // &name\n  | \"ALIAS\"              // *name\n  | \"TAG\"                // !tag\n  | \"INDENT\"             // indentation change\n  | \"NEWLINE\"            // line break\n  | \"COMMENT\"            // # comment\n  | \"EOF\";               // end of file\n\nexport interface Token {\n  type: TokenType;\n  value: string;\n  position: Position;\n  indent: number;        // indentation level (spaces)\n}\n\n// Validation errors with location\nexport interface YamlError {\n  message: string;\n  position: Position;\n  context?: string;      // surrounding text for context\n}\n\n// Result of validation\nexport type ValidationResult =\n  | { valid: true }\n  | { valid: false; error: YamlError };\n```\n\n### 3.2 Lexer Design (`src/yaml/lexer.ts`)\n\nThe lexer performs single-pass tokenization with position tracking.\n\n**Key Responsibilities:**\n- Track current position (line, column, offset)\n- Emit tokens with position information\n- Handle indentation as significant whitespace\n- Detect and report lexical errors (unclosed quotes, invalid characters)\n\n**Lexer State:**\n```typescript\ninterface LexerState {\n  input: string;\n  position: Position;\n  tokens: Token[];\n}\n```\n\n**Tokenization Rules (priority order):**\n\n| Pattern | Token Type | Notes |\n|---------|------------|-------|\n| `---` at line start | DOCUMENT_START | Only at line beginning |\n| `...` at line start | DOCUMENT_END | Only at line beginning |\n| `#.*$` | COMMENT | Consume to end of line |\n| `\\n` | NEWLINE | Increment line, reset column |\n| `^[ ]+` | INDENT | Leading spaces only |\n| `- ` | SEQUENCE_ENTRY | Dash followed by space |\n| `[^:\\n]+:` | MAPPING_KEY | Key followed by colon |\n| `\"[^\"]*\"` | QUOTED_SCALAR | Double-quoted string |\n| `'[^']*'` | QUOTED_SCALAR | Single-quoted string |\n| `\\|` | LITERAL_BLOCK | Literal block indicator |\n| `>` | FOLDED_BLOCK | Folded block indicator |\n| `&\\w+` | ANCHOR | Anchor definition |\n| `\\*\\w+` | ALIAS | Alias reference |\n| `!\\S+` | TAG | Tag indicator |\n| `[^\\n:]+` | SCALAR | Unquoted scalar value |\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Unclosed quoted strings: Report position of opening quote\n- Invalid UTF-8: Report byte position\n- Unexpected characters: Report exact position\n\n### 3.3 Parser Design (`src/yaml/parser.ts`)\n\nThe parser validates the token stream against YAML syntax rules without building an AST.\n\n**Validation Approach:**\n- Stream-based validation (no full AST construction)\n- Track indentation stack for nesting validation\n- Fail-fast on first error\n\n**Parser State:**\n```typescript\ninterface ParserState {\n  tokens: Token[];\n  current: number;           // current token index\n  indentStack: number[];     // stack of indentation levels\n}\n```\n\n**Syntax Rules Validated:**\n\n| Rule | Description | Error Message |\n|------|-------------|---------------|\n| Consistent indentation | Spaces only, consistent within document | \"Inconsistent indentation\" |\n| Valid nesting | Child nodes more indented than parent | \"Invalid indentation: expected at least N spaces\" |\n| Mapping structure | Key must be followed by value or newline | \"Expected value after mapping key\" |\n| Sequence structure | Dash must be followed by value or newline | \"Expected value after sequence indicator\" |\n| Block scalar content | Content must be more indented than indicator | \"Block scalar content must be indented\" |\n| Balanced quotes | All quotes must be closed | \"Unclosed quoted string\" |\n| Valid document markers | `---` and `...` only at document boundaries | \"Unexpected document marker\" |\n\n**Indentation Validation Algorithm:**\n```\n1. Initialize indentStack with [0]\n2. For each INDENT token:\n   a. If indent > stack.top: push (entering nested block)\n   b. If indent == stack.top: continue (same level)\n   c. If indent < stack.top: pop until match found\n   d. If no match: ERROR (invalid dedent)\n```\n\n### 3.4 CLI Design (`src/cli/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\n**Entry Point Logic:**\n```typescript\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  // 1. Parse arguments\n  const filePath = process.argv[2];\n  if (!filePath) {\n    console.error(\"Usage: bun run src/cli/validate-yaml.ts <file>\");\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  // 2. Check file exists\n  const file = Bun.file(filePath);\n  if (!(await file.exists())) {\n    console.error(`Error: File not found: ${filePath}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  // 3. Read and validate\n  const content = await file.text();\n  const result = validateYaml(content);\n\n  // 4. Output result\n  if (result.valid) {\n    console.log(`Valid YAML: ${filePath}`);\n    process.exit(0);\n  } else {\n    const { error } = result;\n    console.error(\n      `${filePath}:${error.position.line}:${error.position.column}: ${error.message}`\n    );\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Error Output Format:**\n```\n<filepath>:<line>:<column>: <error message>\n```\n\nExample:\n```\nconfig.yaml:15:8: Unexpected indentation\n```\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Category | Technology | Rationale |\n|----------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Project standard, fast startup |\n| Language | TypeScript | Project standard, type safety |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() | Native Bun API, async support |\n| Testing | bun:test | Project standard test runner |\n| Dependencies | None added | Requirement: no new dependencies |\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Effort |\n|---|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| T1 | Type definitions | Create `src/yaml/types.ts` with Token, Position, Error types | Small |\n| T2 | Lexer implementation | Create `src/yaml/lexer.ts` with tokenization logic | Medium |\n| T3 | Parser implementation | Create `src/yaml/parser.ts` with validation logic | Medium |\n| T4 | CLI entry point | Create `src/cli/validate-yaml.ts` with main function | Small |\n| T5 | Lexer tests | Create `src/yaml/lexer.test.ts` | Small |\n| T6 | Parser tests | Create `src/yaml/parser.test.ts` | Small |\n| T7 | Integration tests | Create `src/cli/validate-yaml.test.ts` | Small |\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation types, no dependencies\n2. [T2] - Lexer depends only on types\n3. [T3, T5] - Parser needs lexer; lexer tests need lexer (independent of each other)\n4. [T4, T6] - CLI needs parser; parser tests need parser (independent of each other)\n5. [T7] - Integration tests require complete CLI\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (data: lexer uses Token, Position types)\n- T3 -> T2 (interface: parser consumes Token[] from lexer)\n- T4 -> T3 (interface: CLI calls parser validate function)\n- T5 -> T2 (build: tests import lexer module)\n- T6 -> T3 (build: tests import parser module)\n- T7 -> T4 (build: integration tests run CLI)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3 -> T4 -> T7\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Valuable (design tests for) | Avoid |\n|-----------------------------|-------|\n| Lexer tokenization of YAML constructs | Testing regex library behavior |\n| Parser indentation validation | Testing Bun.file() functionality |\n| Error message format and position accuracy | Testing process.exit() mechanics |\n| CLI argument handling | Testing console.log/error output format |\n| Empty file and comment-only file handling | - |\n\n### 7.2 Lexer Tests (`src/yaml/lexer.test.ts`)\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Empty input | `` | [EOF] |\n| Comment only | `# comment` | [COMMENT, EOF] |\n| Simple scalar | `hello` | [SCALAR, EOF] |\n| Mapping | `key: value` | [MAPPING_KEY, SCALAR, EOF] |\n| Sequence | `- item` | [SEQUENCE_ENTRY, SCALAR, EOF] |\n| Nested mapping | `a:\\n  b: c` | [MAPPING_KEY, NEWLINE, INDENT, MAPPING_KEY, SCALAR, EOF] |\n| Quoted string | `\"hello\"` | [QUOTED_SCALAR, EOF] |\n| Unclosed quote | `\"hello` | LexerError at position |\n| Document markers | `---\\ndata\\n...` | [DOCUMENT_START, NEWLINE, SCALAR, NEWLINE, DOCUMENT_END, EOF] |\n\n### 7.3 Parser Tests (`src/yaml/parser.test.ts`)\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Empty document | `` | valid: true |\n| Comment only | `# comment` | valid: true |\n| Simple mapping | `key: value` | valid: true |\n| Nested mapping | `a:\\n  b: c` | valid: true |\n| Sequence | `- a\\n- b` | valid: true |\n| Mixed structure | `list:\\n  - item1\\n  - item2` | valid: true |\n| Invalid indentation | `a:\\nb: c` (dedent to non-matching) | valid: false, error with position |\n| Tab character | `\\tkey: value` | valid: false, tabs not allowed |\n\n### 7.4 Integration Tests (`src/cli/validate-yaml.test.ts`)\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected Output | Exit Code |\n|-----------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| Valid file | valid.yaml | \"Valid YAML: valid.yaml\" on stdout | 0 |\n| Invalid file | invalid.yaml | Error message on stderr | 1 |\n| Missing file | nonexistent.yaml | \"File not found\" on stderr | 1 |\n| No argument | (none) | Usage message on stderr | 1 |\n| Empty file | empty.yaml | \"Valid YAML: empty.yaml\" on stdout | 0 |\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Build Configuration\n\nNo build changes required. The CLI runs directly via Bun:\n\n```bash\nbun run src/cli/validate-yaml.ts <file>\n```\n\n### 8.2 Package.json Script (Optional)\n\nAdd convenience script:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/cli/validate-yaml.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUsage:\n```bash\nbun run validate-yaml config.yaml\n```\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | Usage | N/A | Document new CLI command |\n| add | src/yaml/README.md | API | N/A | Document YAML parser module |\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | Parser architecture | Two-phase (lexer + parser) | Clear separation of concerns, easier error reporting | Single-phase regex, recursive descent |\n| D2 | YAML subset | Block style only (no flow sequences/mappings) | Simpler to implement, covers most config files | Full YAML 1.2 support |\n| D3 | AST construction | No AST, stream validation | Simpler, sufficient for syntax validation only | Full AST for potential future features |\n| D4 | Module location | `src/yaml/` and `src/cli/` | Follows existing flat structure, clear separation | Single file, `src/lib/` |\n| D5 | Error reporting | First error only | Matches fail-fast requirement, simpler | Collect all errors |\n| D6 | Indentation | Spaces only, tabs rejected | YAML spec recommends spaces, simpler validation | Support both with conversion |\n\n## YAML 1.2 Subset Supported\n\n### Supported Features\n\n- Document markers (`---`, `...`)\n- Block mappings (key: value)\n- Block sequences (- item)\n- Nested structures via indentation\n- Comments (# comment)\n- Quoted strings (single and double)\n- Unquoted scalars\n- Multi-line literal blocks (`|`)\n- Multi-line folded blocks (`>`)\n- Null values (null, ~, empty)\n- Boolean values (true, false)\n- Numeric values (integers, floats)\n\n### Not Supported (Out of Scope)\n\n- Flow style collections (`[a, b]`, `{a: b}`)\n- Anchors and aliases (`&anchor`, `*alias`)\n- Tags (`!tag`, `!!str`)\n- Multiple documents in single file (only first document validated)\n- Complex mapping keys\n- Merge keys (`<<`)\n- Binary data\n"
