        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/6f34a28f/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator/tasks.md",
        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 9 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-31\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator built from scratch without external dependencies. The validator uses a two-phase approach: a lexer tokenizes the input file, then a parser validates the token stream against YAML 1.2 syntax rules. The architecture prioritizes simplicity, clear error reporting, and alignment with existing project patterns.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation types, no dependencies\n2. [T2] - Lexer depends only on types\n3. [T3, T5] - Parser needs lexer; lexer tests need lexer (independent of each other)\n4. [T4, T6] - CLI needs parser; parser tests need parser (independent of each other)\n5. [T7] - Integration tests require complete CLI\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (data: lexer uses Token, Position types)\n- T3 -> T2 (interface: parser consumes Token[] from lexer)\n- T4 -> T3 (interface: CLI calls parser validate function)\n- T5 -> T2 (build: tests import lexer module)\n- T6 -> T3 (build: tests import parser module)\n- T7 -> T4 (build: integration tests run CLI)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3 -> T4 -> T7\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation Types\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create type definitions for YAML validator in `src/yaml/types.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-type-definitions-srcyamltypests](design.md#31-type-definitions-srcyamltypests)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Position interface defined with line, column, and offset fields\n    - [ ] TokenType union type defined with all 16 token types (DOCUMENT_START, DOCUMENT_END, MAPPING_KEY, MAPPING_VALUE, SEQUENCE_ENTRY, SCALAR, QUOTED_SCALAR, LITERAL_BLOCK, FOLDED_BLOCK, ANCHOR, ALIAS, TAG, INDENT, NEWLINE, COMMENT, EOF)\n    - [ ] Token interface defined with type, value, position, and indent fields\n    - [ ] YamlError interface defined with message, position, and optional context fields\n    - [ ] ValidationResult union type defined with valid/invalid states\n    - [ ] All types are exported for use by lexer and parser modules\n\n### Lexer Implementation\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement YAML lexer in `src/yaml/lexer.ts` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-lexer-design-srcyamllexerts](design.md#32-lexer-design-srcyamllexerts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Exports tokenize function that accepts string input and returns Token[]\n    - [ ] Tracks position (line, column, offset) for each token\n    - [ ] Handles indentation as significant whitespace (INDENT tokens)\n    - [ ] Tokenizes document markers (--- and ...) at line start\n    - [ ] Tokenizes comments (# to end of line)\n    - [ ] Tokenizes mapping keys (key:) and sequence entries (- item)\n    - [ ] Tokenizes quoted strings (single and double quotes)\n    - [ ] Tokenizes block scalar indicators (| and >)\n    - [ ] Tokenizes unquoted scalar values\n    - [ ] Detects and reports lexical errors (unclosed quotes) with position\n    - [ ] Always emits EOF token at end of input\n\n### Parser Implementation\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement YAML parser/validator in `src/yaml/parser.ts` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-parser-design-srcyamlparserts](design.md#33-parser-design-srcyamlparserts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Exports validate function that accepts Token[] and returns ValidationResult\n    - [ ] Validates consistent indentation (spaces only, no tabs)\n    - [ ] Validates proper nesting via indentation stack algorithm\n    - [ ] Validates mapping structure (key followed by value or newline)\n    - [ ] Validates sequence structure (dash followed by value or newline)\n    - [ ] Validates block scalar content indentation\n    - [ ] Validates document markers appear only at document boundaries\n    - [ ] Fails fast on first error with accurate position information\n    - [ ] Returns { valid: true } for syntactically correct YAML\n    - [ ] Returns { valid: false, error: YamlError } for invalid YAML\n\n### CLI Entry Point\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Implement CLI entry point in `src/cli/validate-yaml.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-cli-design-srcclivalidate-yamlts](design.md#34-cli-design-srcclivalidate-yamlts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Accepts file path as command-line argument (process.argv[2])\n    - [ ] Displays usage message and exits with code 1 when no argument provided\n    - [ ] Checks file existence using Bun.file() API\n    - [ ] Displays \"File not found\" error and exits with code 1 for missing files\n    - [ ] Reads file content and passes to lexer then parser\n    - [ ] Outputs \"Valid YAML: <filepath>\" to stdout and exits with code 0 for valid files\n    - [ ] Outputs error in format \"<filepath>:<line>:<column>: <message>\" to stderr and exits with code 1 for invalid files\n    - [ ] Handles empty files as valid YAML\n\n### Lexer Tests\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Create lexer unit tests in `src/yaml/lexer.test.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#72-lexer-tests-srcyamllexertestts](design.md#72-lexer-tests-srcyamllexertestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test empty input returns [EOF]\n    - [ ] Test comment only input returns [COMMENT, EOF]\n    - [ ] Test simple scalar returns [SCALAR, EOF]\n    - [ ] Test mapping (key: value) returns correct token sequence\n    - [ ] Test sequence (- item) returns correct token sequence\n    - [ ] Test nested mapping with indentation returns correct tokens including INDENT\n    - [ ] Test quoted strings (single and double) return QUOTED_SCALAR\n    - [ ] Test unclosed quote returns LexerError with position\n    - [ ] Test document markers (--- and ...) return correct tokens\n    - [ ] All tests use bun:test framework\n\n### Parser Tests\n\n- [ ] **T6**: Create parser unit tests in `src/yaml/parser.test.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#73-parser-tests-srcyamlparsertestts](design.md#73-parser-tests-srcyamlparsertestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test empty document returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test comment-only document returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test simple mapping returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test nested mapping returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test sequence returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test mixed structure (mapping with sequence values) returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test invalid indentation returns valid: false with error position\n    - [ ] Test tab character returns valid: false (tabs not allowed)\n    - [ ] All tests use bun:test framework\n\n### Integration Tests\n\n- [ ] **T7**: Create integration tests in `src/cli/validate-yaml.test.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#74-integration-tests-srcclivalidate-yamltestts](design.md#74-integration-tests-srcclivalidate-yamltestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test valid YAML file outputs success message to stdout and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Test invalid YAML file outputs error message to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Test missing file outputs \"File not found\" to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Test no argument outputs usage message to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Test empty file outputs success message and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Tests create temporary fixture files for validation scenarios\n    - [ ] All tests use bun:test framework\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Create documentation for README.md - Usage `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Usage\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New Usage section created in README.md\n    - [ ] Documents CLI command syntax: `bun run src/cli/validate-yaml.ts <file>`\n    - [ ] Includes example valid and invalid file outputs\n    - [ ] Documents exit codes (0 for valid, 1 for invalid)\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Create documentation for src/yaml/README.md - API `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: src/yaml/README.md\n\n    **Section**: (new file)\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New file created at src/yaml/README.md\n    - [ ] Documents module purpose (YAML syntax validation)\n    - [ ] Documents exported functions (tokenize, validate)\n    - [ ] Documents type definitions (Token, Position, YamlError, ValidationResult)\n    - [ ] Includes usage examples for programmatic API\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n- [ ] REQ-001: Command accepts a single positional argument for the file path\n- [ ] REQ-001: File path can be absolute or relative to current working directory\n- [ ] REQ-001: Missing file path argument results in appropriate error message and exit code 1\n- [ ] REQ-002: Non-existent file results in error message indicating file not found\n- [ ] REQ-002: Error message includes the file path that was not found\n- [ ] REQ-002: Exit code is 1 for non-existent files\n- [ ] REQ-003: Valid YAML syntax is recognized and accepted\n- [ ] REQ-003: Common YAML constructs are supported: mappings, sequences, scalars, comments, multi-line strings\n- [ ] REQ-003: Parser is implemented without external YAML parsing libraries\n- [ ] REQ-004: Error output includes line number (1-indexed)\n- [ ] REQ-004: Error output includes column number (1-indexed)\n- [ ] REQ-004: Line and column accurately point to the location of the syntax error\n- [ ] REQ-005: Error messages are human-readable plain text\n- [ ] REQ-005: Errors are written to stderr\n- [ ] REQ-005: Format includes file path, line number, column number, and error description\n- [ ] REQ-006: Success message indicates the file is valid YAML\n- [ ] REQ-006: Success message is written to stdout\n- [ ] REQ-006: Message includes the validated file path\n- [ ] REQ-007: Exit code is exactly 0 for valid YAML files\n- [ ] REQ-007: Exit code 0 is returned regardless of YAML content complexity\n- [ ] REQ-008: Exit code is exactly 1 for invalid YAML files\n- [ ] REQ-008: Exit code is 1 for file access errors\n- [ ] REQ-008: Exit code is 1 for missing arguments\n- [ ] REQ-009: No new entries added to package.json dependencies\n- [ ] REQ-009: No new entries added to package.json devDependencies\n- [ ] REQ-009: YAML parsing logic is implemented from scratch\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n- [ ] All tests pass (`bun test`)\n- [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n"
      },
