# YAML Module

YAML syntax validation without external dependencies.

## Exports

### Types (`types.ts`)

```typescript
import { Position, Token, TokenType, YamlError, ValidationResult } from "./types";
```

- `Position` - Line, column, and offset tracking
- `Token` - Lexer output with type, value, position, indent
- `TokenType` - Union of 16 token types
- `YamlError` - Error with message and position
- `ValidationResult` - `{ valid: true }` or `{ valid: false, error: YamlError }`

### Lexer (`lexer.ts`)

```typescript
import { tokenize, LexerError } from "./lexer";

const tokens = tokenize(yamlString);
```

Tokenizes YAML input into an array of tokens. Throws `LexerError` for lexical errors (e.g., unclosed quotes).

### Parser (`parser.ts`)

```typescript
import { validate } from "./parser";

const result = validate(tokens);
if (result.valid) {
  console.log("Valid YAML");
} else {
  console.error(`Error at ${result.error.position.line}:${result.error.position.column}`);
}
```

Validates token stream against YAML syntax rules. Returns validation result with error position on failure.

## Example

```typescript
import { tokenize } from "./lexer";
import { validate } from "./parser";

const yaml = `
name: example
items:
  - one
  - two
`;

const tokens = tokenize(yaml);
const result = validate(tokens);
// result.valid === true
```

