        "content": "# Requirements: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a simple YAML validator command to the project that validates YAML syntax without adding new external dependencies.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1: YAML Validation Function\n- **Description**: Create a function that validates YAML syntax\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Function accepts a YAML string as input\n  - Returns validation result with success/failure status\n  - Returns error details (line number, message) on failure\n  - Handles empty input gracefully\n\n### FR-2: Basic YAML Syntax Support\n- **Description**: Support core YAML syntax validation\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Validates key-value pairs\n  - Validates nested objects (indentation-based)\n  - Validates arrays/lists\n  - Validates multiline strings\n  - Detects common errors: bad indentation, duplicate keys, invalid characters\n\n### FR-3: Command-Line Interface\n- **Description**: Expose validator as a CLI command\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Accept file path as argument\n  - Accept stdin input\n  - Output clear success/failure message\n  - Exit with appropriate codes (0 for success, 1 for failure)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### NFR-1: No External Dependencies\n- **Description**: Implementation must not add new npm packages\n- **Rationale**: User explicitly requested no new dependencies\n- **Constraint**: Use only built-in Bun/Node APIs and hand-written parsing\n\n### NFR-2: TypeScript Implementation\n- **Description**: All code must be written in TypeScript\n- **Rationale**: Consistent with existing codebase\n\n## Scope Boundaries\n\n### In Scope\n- Basic YAML syntax validation\n- Error reporting with line numbers\n- CLI interface for file/stdin validation\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Full YAML 1.2 spec compliance\n- YAML schema validation\n- YAML transformation/manipulation\n- Custom tag support\n- Anchors and aliases support\n\n## User Stories\n\n### US-1: Developer validates YAML file\nAs a developer, I want to validate a YAML file from the command line so that I can catch syntax errors before using the file.\n\n### US-2: Developer validates YAML from stdin\nAs a developer, I want to pipe YAML content to the validator so that I can validate dynamically generated YAML.\n"
