        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/f4c1cefd/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator/design.md",
        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nThe YAML validator will be implemented as a simple, dependency-free module with three main components:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    CLI Entry Point                       │\n│                  (src/yaml-validator.ts)                 │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    Validator Module                      │\n│                  (src/yaml-validate.ts)                  │\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐     │\n│  │   Lexer     │→ │   Parser    │→ │  Validator  │     │\n│  │ (tokenize)  │  │ (structure) │  │  (semantic) │     │\n│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Component Design\n\n### 1. YAML Validator Module (`src/yaml-validate.ts`)\n\n**Purpose**: Core validation logic without external dependencies.\n\n**Approach**: Implement a lightweight YAML parser that tokenizes and validates the structure. Rather than building a full YAML parser, we focus on detecting syntax errors.\n\n**Key Functions**:\n\n```typescript\ninterface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n\ninterface ValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n\nexport function validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;\n```\n\n**Validation Strategy**:\n\n1. **Line-by-line analysis**: Process YAML line by line\n2. **Indentation tracking**: Track indentation levels to detect structure\n3. **Syntax checking**: Validate key-value pairs, lists, and nested structures\n4. **Error accumulation**: Collect all errors rather than failing on first\n\n**Checks Performed**:\n- Consistent indentation (spaces only, consistent width)\n- Valid key format (no special chars at start without quotes)\n- Proper colon placement for key-value pairs\n- List item format (dash followed by space)\n- Unclosed quotes\n- Tabs vs spaces (YAML requires spaces)\n- Trailing content after document markers\n\n### 2. CLI Entry Point (`src/yaml-validator.ts`)\n\n**Purpose**: Command-line interface for the validator.\n\n**Usage**:\n```bash\nbun run src/yaml-validator.ts <file>     # Validate file\ncat file.yaml | bun run src/yaml-validator.ts -  # Validate stdin\n```\n\n**Implementation**:\n```typescript\n// Read from file or stdin\n// Call validateYaml()\n// Output result\n// Exit with appropriate code\n```\n\n### 3. Test Suite (`src/yaml-validate.test.ts`)\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid simple YAML\n- Valid nested YAML\n- Valid arrays\n- Invalid: tab characters\n- Invalid: inconsistent indentation\n- Invalid: unclosed quotes\n- Invalid: duplicate keys at same level\n- Empty input handling\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### D1: No Full YAML Parser\n**Decision**: Implement validation-focused checks rather than full parsing\n**Rationale**: Full YAML spec is complex; validation needs are simpler\n**Trade-off**: Won't catch all edge cases but covers common errors\n\n### D2: Line-Based Processing\n**Decision**: Process YAML line by line\n**Rationale**: Simpler implementation, good error line reporting\n**Trade-off**: Multi-line strings need special handling\n\n### D3: Error Accumulation\n**Decision**: Report all errors, not just first\n**Rationale**: Better developer experience\n**Trade-off**: Slightly more complex implementation\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── yaml-validate.ts      # Core validation logic\n├── yaml-validate.test.ts # Tests for validator\n├── yaml-validator.ts     # CLI entry point\n├── index.ts              # Existing entry point\n├── utils.ts              # Existing utilities\n└── utils.test.ts         # Existing tests\n```\n\n## API Design\n\n### Public API\n\n```typescript\n// Main validation function\nexport function validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;\n\n// Types\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n\nexport interface ValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n```\n\n## Error Messages\n\n| Error Type | Message Format |\n|------------|----------------|\n| Tab character | \"Tab character found; YAML requires spaces for indentation\" |\n| Inconsistent indent | \"Inconsistent indentation: expected {n} spaces, found {m}\" |\n| Invalid key | \"Invalid key format: keys cannot start with '{char}'\" |\n| Unclosed quote | \"Unclosed quote starting at column {n}\" |\n| Missing colon | \"Expected ':' after key\" |\n| Duplicate key | \"Duplicate key '{key}' at this level\" |\n\n## Integration Points\n\n### package.json Script\nAdd convenience script:\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/yaml-validator.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n1. **No new dependencies**: All code hand-written in TypeScript\n2. **Bun runtime**: Use Bun APIs for file/stdin reading\n3. **Existing patterns**: Follow existing code style in the project\n"
